own `Check for Dental Visit`/`Wait for Dental Visit` pair sets
`dental_referral` once (`Dental Referral`'s own `SetAttribute`) and
never clears it anywhere in the file, so any walk that ever reaches that
branch loops for the rest of the patient's simulated life and eventually
exceeds the interpreter's own 10,000-step `max-steps` backstop --
confirmed this session BOTH through `engine/run` (300 patients, three
different `:module-horizon-days` values, all three throwing) AND at the
SAME interpreter layer the census itself walks (`run-module` directly,
registration age 30, 50-year horizon, matching `census.clj`'s own
parameters exactly): 4 of 120 well-mixed-seed walks throw the identical
`max-steps` exception on `:check-for-dental-visit`. The census's own
three-seed sample (`gap {:walk-errors []}` for `injuries`) simply never
sampled this ~3.3%-of-walks branch -- a real gap the census's narrow
sample missed, not a defect in the census itself, and not a config/
horizon-tuning matter (three horizons tried, same failure every time).
Per AR-VB1-6's own fence (no loader/interpreter/engine changes this
session), `injuries.json` and its four genuinely NEW closure members
(`injuries.json` itself, `injuries/broken_jaw.json`, `snf/skilled_
